# review-empty: the agent's branch turns scripts/ into a package with an empty __init__.py,
# touches app/service.py and worker/main.go, and adds an empty py.typed, the review's last file.
# c stops on every file in turn, the empty ones included, and ticks each as it leaves it; the
# last c ticks py.typed and ends the review. C walks back through them the same way. An empty
# file's stop says `empty file, added` and `c  next file` where its text would be. Then a branch
# that deletes an empty scripts/__init__.py, its first file: the review opens on it (#720). Last, a
# branch that moves scripts/refund_by_hand.py without changes: its stop shows the move (#746).
# Then a second round of typed, after the author changes worker/main.go: the review opens on it,
# c passes over the files ticked in the first round, and a reopened review with every file ticked
# says `all files viewed` (#824). Then a branch that moves scripts/refund_by_hand.py and edits
# it: its stop heads the text with the old and new path (#885). Last, a third round of typed: `C`
# passes over the files ticked before, and with every file ticked `c` walks them all again (#823).
merl README.md
wait # orders
run git switch -q -c typed && : > scripts/__init__.py && : > py.typed && printf '\n# Refunds go through the service.\n' >> app/service.py && printf '\n// Retries back off: see the queue.\n' >> worker/main.go && git add -A && git commit -qm typed
merl --review
wait hunk 1/1  file 1/4
caption c stops on the empty scripts/__init__.py like on any other file, and says it is empty (#720)
key c
wait scripts/__init__.py  1:1
key c
wait hunk 1/1  file 3/4
caption the review's last file is empty: c opens it, c again ticks it and ends the review
key c
wait py.typed  1:1
key c
wait last hunk of the review
caption C walks back through the empty file too
key C C
wait scripts/__init__.py  1:1
caption a review whose first file is deleted opens on it: here an empty one (#720)
run git switch -q main && : > scripts/__init__.py && git add -A && git commit -qm init && git push -q origin main && git switch -q -c ungone && git rm -q scripts/__init__.py && printf '\n// Retries back off: see the queue.\n' >> worker/main.go && git commit -qam ungone
merl --review
wait empty file, deleted
caption a file moved without changes shows its old and new path in place of its text (#746)
run git switch -q main && git switch -q -c moved && mkdir -p tools && git mv scripts/refund_by_hand.py tools/refund_by_hand.py && printf '\n// Retries back off: see the queue.\n' >> worker/main.go && git commit -qam moved
merl --review
wait renamed, no changes
key c
wait hunk 1/1  file 2/2
caption a second round of typed: the author fixed worker/main.go since its tick, and the review opens on it (#824)
run git switch -q typed && printf '// Jitter spreads the retries.\n' >> worker/main.go && git commit -qam jitter
merl --review
wait hunk 1/1  file 3/4
caption c passes over py.typed, ticked in the first round: the review ends there (#824)
key c
wait last hunk of the review
caption every file ticked, a reopened review opens on the first and says so (#824)
merl --review
wait all files viewed
caption a file moved and edited heads its text with the old and new path, on every hunk (#885)
run git switch -q main && git switch -q -c moved-edited && mkdir -p tools && git mv scripts/refund_by_hand.py tools/refund_by_hand.py && printf '\n# Run it once per refund.\n' >> tools/refund_by_hand.py && git commit -qam moved-edited
merl --review
wait scripts/refund_by_hand.py  →  tools/refund_by_hand.py
caption a third round of typed, worker/main.go fixed again: C from it passes over the files ticked before (#823)
run git switch -q typed && printf '// Five retries at most.\n' >> worker/main.go && git commit -qam five
merl --review
wait hunk 1/1  file 3/4
key C
wait first hunk of the review
key c
wait last hunk of the review
caption every file ticked: c walks them all from the first again (#823)
merl --review
wait all files viewed
key c
wait scripts/__init__.py  1:1
